    "topic_title": "Logarithmic Expressions",
    "stem": "What is the exact value of log₄(1/8)?",
    "choices": [
     {
      "choice_key": "A",
      "choice_text": "3/2",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Reciprocal sign error: 3/2 is the exponent that makes 4 raised to that power equal 8, not 1/8. Fix: Check whether your proposed exponent produces the argument or its reciprocal."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "B",
      "choice_text": "−2/3",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Base–argument reversal: −2/3 is the exponent in (1/8)ʸ = 4, not in 4ʸ = 1/8. Fix: Rewrite the logarithm with its base as the exponential base."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "C",
      "choice_text": "−3/2",
      "is_correct": true,
      "rationale": "The value is the exponent y satisfying 4ʸ = 1/8. Since 4 = 2² and 1/8 = 2⁻³, this becomes 2²ʸ = 2⁻³, so 2y = −3 and y = −3/2."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "D",
      "choice_text": "−3",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "Base substitution error: 2⁻³ = 1/8, but the logarithm has base 4, not base 2. Since 4⁻³ = 1/64, −3 does not work. Fix: Raise the stated base to your proposed exponent and compare with the argument."
     }
    ]
   },
